.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt AUTODO-EVENTD 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm autodo-eventd
.Nd companion daemon for the mac_do_auto MAC policy module
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl config Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl Fl log Ns = Ns Ar path
.Op Fl Fl check-abi
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
manages the runtime policy of the
.Xr mac_do_auto 4
kernel module and consumes its audit events.
At startup, and again whenever the configuration changes, it reads the
.Xr autodo.conf 5
configuration file, resolves group names and policy profiles, compiles
privilege bitmaps, and pushes the result to the kernel module through
.Pa /dev/autodo .
It then monitors
.Pa /dev/autodo
for audit events, appending them as JSON lines to the audit log.
.Pp
The daemon runs in the foreground; the
.Pa autodo_eventd
rc script supervises it with
.Xr daemon 8 .
.Pp
At startup it reads the module's ABI version and exits if it differs from
its own.
The ioctl commands carry their parameter size, so a change to the
interface changes the command numbers: a daemon paired with a module from
another release would fail every policy push and leave the kernel with
whatever policy it already had, which in legacy mode is the default scope
.Dq all .
Package upgrades replace the files but leave the previous module resident,
so reload it with
.Xr kldunload 8
and
.Xr kldload 8 ,
or reboot.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl Flconfig Ns = Ns Ar path
Configuration file
(default:
.Pa /usr/local/etc/autodo/autodo.conf ) .
.It Fl Fl log Ns = Ns Ar path
Audit log file
(default:
.Pa /var/log/autodo/events.json ) .
.It Fl Fl check-abi
Report whether the loaded module's ABI matches this daemon, then exit.
Useful after a package upgrade to confirm the module was reloaded.
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload the configuration file and re-push policy to the kernel.
The configuration file is also watched for changes and reloaded
automatically.
.It Dv SIGTERM
Shut down cleanly.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/autodo/autodo.conf
Configuration file.
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/autodo/profiles/
Directory of named policy profiles referenced by the configuration.
.It Pa /var/log/autodo/events.json
Audit event log (JSON lines).
.It Pa /dev/autodo
Kernel module control and event device.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac_do_auto 4 ,
.Xr autodo.conf 5 ,
.Xr daemon 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Daniel Morante Aq Mt daniel@morante.net
